<head>
<%- include('partials/head', { meta: { title: 'Privacy Policy | GetQuotationMaker', desc: 'What GetQuotationMaker does with your data: quote details sent to build your PDF, what stays in your browser, payments and licence checks, and who else receives data.', path: '/privacy' } }) %>
</head>
<body>
<%- include('partials/nav') %>
<header class="hero">
  <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
  <p class="lead">GetQuotationMaker has no accounts and no advertising. It counts page visits, Get Pro clicks and a few quote tool steps as daily totals, with no cookies and nothing that identifies you. This page lists the data the site handles, where it goes and why.</p>
  <p class="meta">Last updated: 19 November 2026</p>
</header>

<main class="article">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>GetQuotationMaker (www.getquotationmaker.com) is run by Peak Apps Studio. For any question about your data, email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>When you make a quote</h2>
    <p>The form and the live preview run in your browser. When you press a download button, your browser sends the quote to our server, which builds the PDF. The request contains what you typed: your business name, email address and postal address, your client's name, email address and postal address, the quote number and dates, the line items, prices, tax and discount, your notes and terms, and your logo if you added one.</p>
    <p>The server builds the PDF in memory, sends it back to your browser and does not keep a copy of the quote, unless you send it for acceptance with Pro (see &ldquo;Quotes sent for acceptance&rdquo; below). If a PDF fails to build, the server writes a technical error message to our hosting logs.</p>

    <h2 id="acceptance-links">Quotes sent for acceptance (Pro)</h2>
    <p>With Pro you can press &ldquo;Send for acceptance&rdquo;. It is the one case in which we keep a quote, so here is what happens to it.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What is stored.</strong> A snapshot of the quote as it is in the form when you press the button: everything that goes into the PDF (your business name, email address and postal address, your client's name, email address and postal address, the line items, prices, tax, notes and terms) and your logo, made smaller if it is large. A snapshot is at most about 200 KB. We also store the times the link was made and first opened. When your client accepts, we store the name they type, the note if they add one, and the time in UTC. If you give an email address for the acceptance email, we keep it only until that email has been sent, then delete it.</li>
      <li><strong>What is not stored.</strong> Your client's IP address, browser details and cookies. The client's page sets no cookie and runs no script. Your Pro key never reaches the storage: our server turns it into a one-way code that is used only to count how many links one purchase makes (at most 30 in 24 hours).</li>
      <li><strong>Who can see it.</strong> Anyone who has the client link can read the quote, download the PDF and accept it, so send the link only to your client. Anyone who has your status link can see its status, including the name and the note. Each link is made of 128 random bits and cannot be guessed. The client's page asks search engines not to index it and sends no referrer. We do not read quotes. They sit in storage on Cloudflare that only our code opens. The hosting logs of Vercel record the address of each page that is opened, so the client link is in them for as long as Vercel keeps its logs.</li>
      <li><strong>In your browser.</strong> The status links of the quotes you send are kept in this browser's local storage, with the quote number, your client's name and the total, so that the status page can list them. What your client typed is shown on the status page and is not saved there. Clear this site's data in your browser settings, or press &ldquo;Remove from this list&rdquo;, to delete the list.</li>
      <li><strong>How long.</strong> 90 days from the day the link is made. Then the link stops working and the snapshot, the acceptance and everything the client typed are deleted from storage. We cannot bring a record back after that, so download the PDF or keep a copy of the status page if you need one. To have a link deleted sooner, email us the link or the status link.</li>
      <li><strong>The email.</strong> If you gave an address, one plain email goes to it when the quote is accepted, sent through Forward Email. It holds the quote number and a link to your status page, and nothing your client typed.</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>What is stored in your browser</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your own details.</strong> Your business name, email address and postal address are saved in your browser's local storage, so they are filled in next time. They stay on your device until you clear this site's data in your browser settings.</li>
      <li><strong>The Pro cookie.</strong> If you activate Pro, your licence key is saved in a cookie called <code>qm_license</code> so that Pro stays on in that browser. The cookie lasts one year and is sent only to this site. The "Remove Pro from this browser" button on the Activate Pro page deletes it.</li>
      <li><strong>The kind of site that sent you.</strong> One word such as <code>google</code> or <code>direct</code>, kept in this tab's session storage so that a Get Pro click can say where your visit began (see "Visit and Get Pro click counts"). It is deleted when you close the tab.</li>
      <li><strong>The download choice.</strong> A short note in this tab's session storage that the choice between the free and the Pro PDF has already been shown, so that it is shown once per visit and not again. It is deleted when you close the tab.</li>
      <li><strong>Your quote while you pay.</strong> If you press a Get Pro button while your quote has something in it, the form is kept in this tab's session storage so that it is still there when the page reloads with Pro on. It stays in your browser and is not sent to us. It is deleted when the page puts it back, or when you close the tab.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The site sets no other cookies and uses none for tracking or advertising.</p>

    <h2>Licence checks</h2>
    <p>When you enter a licence key on the Activate Pro page, our server sends it to Gumroad's licence service (api.gumroad.com) to confirm that it belongs to a valid purchase that has not been refunded. On later visits the server checks the key again and keeps the answer in its memory for up to six hours. Gumroad's answer includes details of the purchase; we use it only to decide whether Pro is on, and we do not store it.</p>
    <p>A purchase made with Paddle needs no key from you. When the payment is done, the page sends the payment's number to our Pro service (a small program on Cloudflare), which asks Paddle whether it is a valid purchase and answers with a key that our server keeps in the Pro cookie. On later visits the server asks the Pro service about that key again and keeps the answer in its memory for up to six hours. The Pro service stores no email address and no key.</p>

    <h2>Buying Pro</h2>
    <p>Pro is sold by Paddle.com, the seller of record. The Get Pro buttons open Paddle's checkout in a panel on this page; your email address, country and payment details go to Paddle, not to us. Paddle tells us your email address, country and the details of your order, and we use them to answer questions about your purchase and to issue refunds. Paddle emails your receipt, and our Pro service emails you one link that turns Pro on in your other browsers; the Activate Pro page can send that link again to the address you paid with.</p>
    <p>Before November 2026, Pro was sold through Gumroad. Those purchases keep working with their licence key; for them, we received your email address and the details of your order from Gumroad.</p>

    <h2>Visit and Get Pro click counts</h2>
    <p>Most pages send one short note to a counter when they open, and another when you follow a Get Pro link. A note holds the page address (without anything after a ? or #), the part of the page the link was in, and one word for the kind of site that sent you, such as Google, social or direct. It holds no cookie, no IP address, no browser details and nothing that tells one visitor from another. The counter is a small program on Cloudflare that adds one to a daily total for that combination and keeps nothing else. Cloudflare receives the request as any host does, including your IP address, but the counter does not read or store it. The quote tool sends four more notes of the same kind: when a PDF has been made (free or Pro), when a logo has been chosen, when an offer to buy Pro was shown and when its Get Pro button was pressed. Each carries the page address, one word such as free or dialog, and the kind of site, and never the quote, the logo or anything you typed. Some pages send no notes.</p>

    <h2>Fonts</h2>
    <p>The site's fonts load from Google Fonts. To fetch them, your browser connects to Google's servers, which receive your IP address and browser details.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site runs on Vercel. Like any web host, Vercel processes each request, including your IP address, the page you asked for and your browser type, and keeps request logs for a limited time.</p>

    <h2>Emails</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we receive your email address and your message. Mail sent to peakappsstudio.com addresses is forwarded by Forward Email to a Gmail inbox. We use your email only to reply to you.</p>

    <h2>Who else receives data</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Company</th><th>What for</th><th>Privacy policy</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Vercel</td><td>Hosting the site and its server</td><td><a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice" rel="noopener">vercel.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Paddle</td><td>Checkout, payments, sales tax and receipts (seller of record)</td><td><a href="https://www.paddle.com/legal/privacy" rel="noopener">paddle.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Gumroad</td><td>Purchases made before November 2026 and their licence checks</td><td><a href="https://gumroad.com/privacy" rel="noopener">gumroad.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Google</td><td>Web fonts, and the Gmail inbox for our email</td><td><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">policies.google.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Cloudflare</td><td>Running the counter of page visits and Get Pro clicks, the Pro service that checks Paddle purchases, and the storage of quotes sent for acceptance</td><td><a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">cloudflare.com</a></td></tr>
        <tr><td>Forward Email</td><td>Forwarding mail sent to our address, sending the Pro link and sending the acceptance email</td><td><a href="https://forwardemail.net/en/privacy" rel="noopener">forwardemail.net</a></td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>Vercel, Gumroad, Google and Cloudflare are based in the United States and Paddle in the United Kingdom, so your data may be processed there. We do not sell your data, and we do not share it with advertisers.</p>

    <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Quote details: only while the server builds your PDF. A quote you send for acceptance: 90 days, then deleted with what your client typed.</li>
      <li>Details saved in your browser: until you clear them. The Pro cookie expires after one year.</li>
      <li>Licence check results: up to six hours in the server's memory.</li>
      <li>Visit and Get Pro click counts: daily totals with no personal data, kept for up to 400 days.</li>
      <li>Hosting logs: kept by Vercel for a limited time under its own policy.</li>
      <li>Purchase records: kept by Paddle (and, for earlier purchases, by Gumroad) under their own policies.</li>
      <li>Emails: until we delete them. Ask us and we will delete yours, unless we need it as a record of a payment or refund.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask us for a copy of the personal data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, or object to how we use it. Email <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a> and we will reply within one month. We do not keep your quotes, and you can delete what is saved in your browser yourself by clearing this site's data. If you live in the EU or the UK, you can also complain to your local data protection authority.</p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>GetQuotationMaker is a tool for businesses and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If the site starts handling data differently, we will update this page and the date at the top.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Peak Apps Studio, <a href="mailto:info@peakappsstudio.com">info@peakappsstudio.com</a>. See also our <a href="/terms">terms of use</a>.</p>
  </div>
</main>
